# Research Probes

## Purpose

Dev-time reverse engineering and validation. Outputs go to console or DevTree browser — not production overlay.

## Adding a probe

- New flag in `Research/Program.cs` (e.g. `--my-probe`).
- Read via `MemoryReader` + `Poe2Offsets`; print PASS/FAIL/DRIFT clearly.
- Paste-ready offset blocks for copying into `Poe2Offsets.cs` when validated.

## DevTree (`--devtree`)

- `DevTreeServer` + `DevTreeHtml` at `localhost:7778`.
- PoE2 stand-in for ExileApi DevTree — memory/UI/entity explorer.

## Atlas recovery

- `--atlas-probe`: one-shot projection recovery when atlas is open.
- `--atlas-graph`: node graph + connection vector validation.

## Rules

- **Never** add Research as a dependency of Overlay.
- Probes may be messy; overlay code may not. Validate here, integrate cleanly in Core/Overlay.
- Document probe usage in `AGENTS.md` when adding significant new commands.
